== file input/a.md
# a
== stdout
Print a compact structural outline of source files

Usage: outln [OPTIONS] <PATH>...

Arguments:
  <PATH>...  Files to outline, or directories and glob patterns for a glob view

Options:
      --debug    Print the source with the parts that became the outline highlighted (debug mode)
  -v, --version  Print the version
  -h, --help     Print help

Modes:
  outln <file>...            Full outline for each file (header, declarations, line ranges).
  outln <dir|glob>...        Glob view: one line per file with its header.
                             Explicit files may be mixed in; they use the same one-line format.
                             Respects .gitignore and .git/info/exclude inside git repositories,
                             .ignore files, and git's global excludes file;
                             skips node_modules, dot entries and symlinks.
  outln --debug <file|dir>   Source text with the extracted outline highlighted.

Examples:
  outln docs/guide.md
  outln docs "src/**/*.md"
  outln --debug docs/guide.md
